{"availability":"available","full":"abubakarsiddik31/golem","name":"golem","description":"Go-first framework for dependable AI agents: typed dependencies and outputs, explicit tools, composable models, observable runs","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":3,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-16T04:38:42Z","updated":"2026-10-06T08:44:59Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://abubakarsiddik31.github.io/golem/","topics":["agent-framework","ai-agents","anthropic","gemini","go","llm","openai"],"demo":"https://abubakarsiddik31.github.io/golem/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T16:28:35.317Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T16:28:35.317Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T16:28:35.317Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T16:28:35.317Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T16:28:35.317Z","stars":3,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A Go-first framework for building dependable, production-grade AI agents.","Compile-time type safety, zero external dependencies, explicit execution control, and deep MCP integration.","Python frameworks like Pydantic AI made agent prototyping accessible with typed schemas and clean ergonomics. However, deploying AI agents to mission-critical production systems demands the strengths of Go: high-throughput concurrency, predictable memory usage, fast execution, small deployment binaries, and compile-time correctness."],"features":["🛡️ Compile-Time Type Safety & Generics: Agents are declared as Agent[Deps, Output]. Tools access strongly-typed dependencies (databases, auth contexts, HTTP clients) via RunContext[Deps]. No map[string]any spaghetti or…","📦 Zero External Dependencies: Built exclusively on Go's standard library. Instant compilation, tiny container images, and a clean security profile free of supply-chain vulnerabilities.","🌐 Provider Agnostic: Native adapters for OpenAI, Anthropic (with prompt caching and thinking signatures), Google Gemini, AWS Bedrock (Converse API with SigV4), Azure OpenAI, and local offline models with Ollama and LM…","🔌 Native Model Context Protocol (MCP): Full-featured MCP client supporting both stdio and streaming HTTP transports, effortlessly turning external MCP servers into typed agent tools.","🔄 Production Resilience & Self-Correction: In-loop model self-correction (ModelRetry), automated multi-model fallbacks, exponential backoff, per-tool deadlines, and clean in-tool cancellation (tool.Canceled)."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/abubakarsiddik31/golem/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"54fbae4a84eafc923695958ab7b6ee61bb30bdfeeba247881fd11b09d2a7efae","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T16:28:35.317Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T16:28:35.317Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A Go-first framework for building dependable, production-grade AI agents.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/abubakarsiddik31/golem/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"54fbae4a84eafc923695958ab7b6ee61bb30bdfeeba247881fd11b09d2a7efae","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/abubakarsiddik31/golem/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T16:28:35.317Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-06T08:44:59Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/abubakarsiddik31/golem/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T16:28:35.317Z","hash":"54fbae4a84eafc923695958ab7b6ee61bb30bdfeeba247881fd11b09d2a7efae","originalBytes":25929,"storedBytes":25929,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["examples","docs","main.go","tool","guides","check","mark","white","agent","run","common","golem","err","model","string","tools","offline","execution","openai","output","mcp","typed","client","providers","skills","history","text","dependencies","nil","struct","type","database","pdf","thinking","token","anthropic","api","cost","http","json","shell","streaming","abubakarsiddik31","adapter","azure","bedrock","command","context","external","gemini","github.c